{{!-- Where a posted item is copied to.

The target is always asked for, never inferred from the selected token or the
assigned character — a player answers one line, and a GM with a shelf of NPCs
does not have to remember what was selected before clicking. The own character
is offered first and preselected, so the common case is still one keystroke.

A plain select rather than the create dialog's portrait cards: this list is
every actor the reader owns, which for a GM is the whole cast, and a native
select is the control that stays usable at that length. --}}

<p class='take-item-prompt'>{{prompt}}</p>

<label class='take-item-target'>
  <span>{{localize 'TNO.Item.Chat.TakeTarget'}}</span>
  <select name='actor' autofocus>
    {{#each actors}}
      <option value='{{this.id}}' {{#if this.selected}}selected{{/if}}>{{this.name}}</option>
    {{/each}}
  </select>
</label>
